            "review_title": "Review at District K",
            "review_text": "Trần T\nHo Chi Minh City, Vietnam10 contributions\n0\nWeak in problem-solving. District Manager K\nAug 2026 • Friends\nToday's story, I give it one star entirely because of the management. When settling the bill, I will pay in cash. I would like to use a card to pay for the bill under 20 million VND to issue an invoice under 20 million VND. I also request assistance in separating the Mac 12 bottle into a different bill so I can issue an invoice under 20 million VND and pay for the bill with the Mac 12 bottle separately in cash. The bill hasn't been fully paid because they refused to split the bill, and I haven't agreed to pay it.\nThe manager responds to customers in a very stiff manner. The bill from your side is out and cannot be separated. I have a request for the accountant to contact me for assistance, and today I received the full bill.\nI sent back 25 million 500 thousand in cash and requested the accountant to contact me tomorrow to assist me in using the payment card, but they haven't contacted me or called me on any number; I can't reach them at 0994301941. They called me at 8:26 this morning, and I called back twice at 11:12.\nBy default, deduct the bill from the cash I give back to the restaurant. A very fun and famous place, but the problem handling is too bad, very bad.\nI also run a restaurant, a sky bar, and a club, and I really don't like the way District K's operations management handles things.\nFor example, if a staff member charges a customer for soft drinks (water, soda, etc.) that are still 100% unused, and the customer forgets to return them, and the bill cannot be separated, does the customer have to pay for the items they haven't used?\nAlong with that, at first we ordered a bottle of Mac 12 and fruit. Later, please add 2 bottles of Mac and 2 plates of fruit to the combo (if the first plate is not keyed in the system, the kitchen will prepare the items, but the bill will only show item 2 bottles of Mac 12 with 2 portions of fruit + 2 portions of chicken cartilage). The problem here is poor operational management.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nTranslated from Vietnamese\nShow original\nWritten August 18, 2026",
